\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379427 1113 #uuid "2748b840-0359-55b1-82e2-d468720777e9" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379427 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x+1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2]-[\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+0]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379429 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379430 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379431 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379432 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379433 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1041 "selection" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379429 13194139536014 true] [17592186379428 1110 #uuid "41a54673-44eb-597a-b477-2c8c96daec96" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379429 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379429 1111 #uuid "abd6f9ba-8bc4-574d-afaa-04d16a680351" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379430 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379430 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379430 1111 #uuid "8bfad427-41a5-52a4-90ae-fb95e9a0ab4f" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379431 1034 "I only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379431 1111 #uuid "697aaea7-cc8f-5a21-897d-be261bed424b" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379432 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379432 1111 #uuid "10b60963-0aa1-51fd-8fd1-c3f7ab235311" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379433 1034 "II only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379433 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379433 1111 #uuid "f107b48e-c3b5-5fdc-8161-ef98f2013fa3" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379435 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1089 "q-158425" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073533/assets/87c5e1b3307b2a42fff6a97408c0475dbe242bef4a9dbfbabcec407b3fa23ce1.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{3},\\, & 0\\le x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1113 #uuid "f0b0485b-974e-561b-8f7e-8240d4d2ce2e" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379434 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379436 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379437 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379438 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379439 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379440 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1041 "selection" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379439 13194139536014 true] [17592186379435 1110 #uuid "de60368d-ae7e-5f26-9f09-787d4665dc4a" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379436 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379436 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379436 1111 #uuid "0ef27a7d-b7e2-5792-8e6b-1484643b34e0" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379437 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379437 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379437 1111 #uuid "60b90ed2-8efe-55b4-ad9a-2a13c8c4b93e" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379438 1034 "I and III only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379438 1111 #uuid "f2324ff1-7596-5acf-836a-21ef3e5ec702" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379439 1034 "I only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379439 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379439 1111 #uuid "25a56bd7-9eb2-519a-806d-81c81efea590" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379440 1034 "II only" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379440 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379440 1111 #uuid "2ee397ee-0d18-50ec-989e-bc21a4b79de5" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379442 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1089 "q-158444" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1100 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{k},\\, & 3\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1113 #uuid "dd8f04ea-bc7c-5600-a918-9219fb398cc5" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379441 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{x}{k}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{x}{k}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2k}]}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =(\\frac{25}{2k}-\\frac{9}{2k}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2k} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{k}=1\\,⟹\\,k=8.\n$$" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379443 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379444 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379445 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379446 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379447 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1041 "selection" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379444 13194139536014 true] [17592186379442 1110 #uuid "fd31ced5-5de1-583c-abfa-e86a8372459a" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379443 1034 "12" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379443 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379443 1111 #uuid "06d50ec8-8818-522f-b6f5-05673b9784a4" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379444 1034 "8" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379444 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379444 1111 #uuid "d958f4d8-57fc-5383-b68b-63f16b3d7a8c" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379445 1034 "2" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379445 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379445 1111 #uuid "1d0a6412-5b49-5359-9aa3-cf5158ba3049" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379446 1034 "6" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379446 1111 #uuid "cfa53ef2-7cc0-52e9-8f0d-8bd9c145c277" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379447 1034 "4" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379447 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379447 1111 #uuid "eb26d6e3-1943-5ed5-849c-7b1854036c9a" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379449 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1089 "q-86915" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1100 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{{x}^{2}},\\, & 2<x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1113 #uuid "3422e9c0-2baf-5d35-9d4c-d22907f92c7a" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379448 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{10}\\frac{k}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{10}\\frac{k}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{10}k{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{k}{x}]}_{2}^{10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k}{10}+\\frac{k}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2k}{5}=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379451 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379452 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379454 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1041 "selection" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379449 1110 #uuid "e1ac95d4-9d42-53f1-abed-a9d99e0b0fa1" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379450 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379450 1111 #uuid "d8d419b6-7d89-59ee-bdf1-076e957cb3f4" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379451 1034 "10" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379451 1111 #uuid "426e6217-15ce-5856-9e89-eaf6e463a4dd" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379452 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379452 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379452 1111 #uuid "f83de66a-c179-5fbc-8759-e545544ed278" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379453 1034 "2" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379453 1111 #uuid "c151d2b4-2690-59b3-bf65-903bf7f5e355" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379454 1034 "5" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536014 true] [17592186379454 1111 #uuid "1723237a-d492-59e5-a297-4133998b7839" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379456 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1089 "q-87151" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1100 "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The number of heads obtained when a coin is flipped twice\n- The height of a randomly selected person, measured in meters\n- The concentration, in grams per cubic centimeter, of glucose in a person's bloodstream" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1113 #uuid "9320a099-8469-5e83-8243-caaa61ac2eb4" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379455 1145 "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073533/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379457 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379458 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379459 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379460 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379461 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1041 "selection" 13194139536014 true] [17592186379456 1104 #edb/ref 1